==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Inspector Gabriel''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Section Chief Gravicci''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

Evolves into '''Arcane Commissioner Gravicci''' at level 60 using [[Catfruit]], [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]], and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Detective Vigler's main use lies in the "Research" Effect UP [[Cat Combo|Combo]] [[Cheating Heart? (Combo)|Cheating Heart?]], which is no less potent than [[Aerial Recon (Combo)|Aerial Recon]] but requires half as many slots, forming a powerful synergy with [[Biohazard (Combo)|Biohazard]], [[Bony Bone (Combo)|Bony Bone]], [[Mini-Saurus (Combo)|Mini-Saurus]] and [[Pork on Rice (Combo)|Pork on Rice]]. In [[battle]], this unit can also be used as a crowd-controller to [[Freeze]] [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] and [[:Category:Alien Enemies|Aliens]] in his first form, and his guaranteed [[Wave Attack]] can occasionally Freeze backliners such as [[Alpacky]] and [[Calamary]], as well as clear peons, although his mediocre DPS and inconsistent Freeze chance keep him from excelling at this role.

His Evolved Form Freezes [[:Category:Zombie Enemies|Zombies]] instead of Floating enemies, but due to his long attack animation and low standing range, they will likely burrow before he can attack. However, he can still be used against slower or non-burrowing Zombies such as [[Lord Gravey]] or [[Zyclone]]. Since waves also carry his [[Zombie Killer]] ability, he can occasionally wipe out a group of weaker Zombies such as [[Zoge]] or [[The Thrillerz]].

His main weakness is his long foreswing and pause between attacks. If he misses a hit or fails to freeze (which is equally as likely as freezing), he may face a lot of damage, plus he won't be able to shake off Zombies who un-burrow on him easily. Thus, Inspector Gabriel's utilities largely go to waste, making him not worth even sending out in most situations.

==='''True Form'''===
His True Form, Section Chief Gravicci, fixes many of his problems as an [[:Category:Anti-Zombie Cats|anti-Zombie]]: [[Strong Against]] provides extra survivability, which, combined with his 6 knockbacks and 98-second recharge time, makes it quite possible to stack a few of him. His attack animation becomes roughly 0.67 seconds faster and he gains a 100% chance to freeze for about 50% uptime.

Strong Against, combined with Freeze, finally turns Gravicci into a competent anti-Zombie, having more than 9K DPS against them at level 30. Gravicci's 6 knockbacks allow him to reposition frequently from Zombies burrowing onto him, and his wave attack allows him to cover large groups of them and even reach backliners such as [[Zamelle]], freezing them and hindering their progress greatly if not outright killing them. It also helps that Gravicci's base DPS is not bad either, allowing him to do well even on mixed stages.

His Wave Attack can reach far into enemy defences, and carries his effects. This allows Gravicci to crowd-control over a wide area, greatly crippling his targeted traits and chipping away at other enemies. One easily overlooked aspect of Gravicci is that his delay between attacks consists solely of backswing, meaning that if he is knocked back in between attacks, he will immediately retaliate, increasing his overall DPS. While difficult to pull off, it is worth baiting enemies into Gravicci's range, taking advantage of his long attack animation to get as many enemies as possible into his attack range before he blasts them all at one go. Overall, a very strong True Form and definitely worth the resources.

==='''Ultra Form'''===
His Ultra Form, Arcane Commissioner Gravicci, gains a few buffs that further enhance his performance as both a generalist and specialist. Most notably, Arcane Commissioner Gravicci's attack animation has one less second of foreswing, allowing him to land attacks leagues more consistently than before. This is especially useful against Zombies, which would at first usually burrow in the middle of Section Chief Gravicci's drawn out foreswing animation, now have more of an opportunity to get interrupted during burrowing due to this change.

Additionally, Arcane Commissioner Gravicci has been kitted out with [[Sage Slayer]]. This helps make him more viable in specific Zero Legends stages, particularly those featuring [[Oldstrich]] (and [[Shachiko]] if you have his Talents unlocked). In practice, this ability is mainly useful for Oldstrich, bypassing his resistance to most other anti-Zombie units' Freeze effects. The advantage against Shachiko is much more dubious, since the primary strategy for handling Shachiko is to burst it down with rushers like [[Idi:N (Special Cat)|Idi:NX]]. Despite this, he's an amazing alternative crowd-controller in stages where you can't accomplish this chain as easily. This ability can also see various cases of application as a general Sage Slayer, outranging [[Doctor K.O.]] and [[Dark Dober]], and using his pierce to strike enemies like [[Prof. Owlbrowley]] or [[Techn-Old Hyena]].

Speaking of his pierce, Arcane Commissioner Gravicci's Wave Attack level has increased to 5, upping his effective range to 1,133. Combined with his faster foreswing, this gives him far greater opportunities to snipe incoming enemies and super-backliners, such as [[Miss Haka]] or [[Golem Sunfish]]. What's more, he himself has gained [[Immune to Waves|Wave Immunity]], which does not impact either of his target traits much at all (except against [[Haniwanwan]], [[Gigahaniwan]] and [[Masked Grandmaster Cat (Enemy)|Masked Grandmaster Cat]] if you decide to invest into talents), but serves as an extremely nice bonus for generalist usage.

Overall, this is truly a very strong Ultra Form, fixing many of Gravicci's former issues and making him a strong, consistent pick for many scenarios and matchups. However, the power held by this Ultra Form is locked behind a [[Catfruit|Gold Catfruit Seed]] (only obtainable from [[Infernal Tower]]'s [[Infernal Tower/Floor 30|Floor 30]]), which faces heavy competition from other units like [[Cat Clan Heroes (Uber Rare Cat)|Heavenly Cat Heroes]]. If you do get the Ultra Form however, you won't be disappointed in the slightest.

==='''Talents'''===
While expensive, '''Target [[:Category:Relic Enemies|Relic]]''' gives Gravicci another target to be '''Strong Against''', increasing his health and DPS while allowing a 100% Freeze chance against them for 5 seconds through his Lv.3 (Lv.5 in Ultra Form) Wave Attack. The stat boosts from Talents increase his health and damage to acceptable levels, allowing him to function well as a generalist. With Relic being one of the most relevant traits in the game, this upgrade allows Gravicci to find value in many people's collections. It helps his case that many Relics are powerful frontline pushers, like [[Relic Bun-Bun]] and [[Oldhorn]], making them vulnerable to his Freeze and high DPS. He can also use them as stepping stones to keep firing off waves, hitting other Relic backliners. His attack power goes even higher against Relics due to his Strong Against, allowing him to destroy entire swarms of Relics while freezing any survivors for an extended period of time. Paired with '''[[Immune to Curse]]''', which prevents his abilities from being shut down by Relics or the [[Relic Doge Base (Enemy Base)|Relic Doge Base]], both Talents convert Gravicci into an excellent [[:Category:Anti-Relic Cats|anti-Relic]] and -Zombie option with crowd-control capabilities, extending his overall usage to [[Uncanny Legends]] stages that feature both types of threats.

As always, do not bother with Resist Freeze as its situationality combined with being a Resist talent and not an immunity make it a major waste of NP. Due to his stat based nature, his Attack and HP buff talents should be considered for investment if you use him often, especially if you have his Ultra Form.
