==Trivia==
*In each form, the floating cat above Vigler/Gabriel/Gravicci resembles a different fictional detective:
**Detective Vigler's cat is dressed as [[wikipedia:Sherlock Holmes|Sherlock Holmes]].
**Inspector Gabriel's cat has the signature hat and bag of [[wikipedia:Kosuke Kindaichi|Kosuke Kindaichi]].
**Section Chief Gravicci's cat references [[wikipedia:Miss Marple|Miss Marple]].
*The names Vigler and Gravicci are derived from ''gravity''. In Vigler's case, this is only obvious in Japanese:
**<u>グラヴィ</u>ティ ''<u>guravi</u>ti'' (gravity) → ヴィグラー ''Vigurā'' (Vigler)
*As a demonic detective often seen upside-down, Vigler may have been inspired by the manga ''[[wikipedia:Neuro: Supernatural Detective|Neuro: Supernatural Detective]]''.
*Detective Vigler's description says he solved just over 665 cases, which means 666, a number commonly referred to as the "Number of the Beast."
*Detective Vigler's Japanese term contains the word 魔界 ''[[wikipedia:ja:魔界|makai]]'' ("demon world"), which is also used in [[The Aku Realms]]' Japanese name. Whether there is any connection is unknown.

